asahi: narrow 16-bit flat fragment inputs from their 32-bit coefficients

Varyings reach the fragment shader as 32-bit values in the coefficient
registers: 0001 widens 16-bit vertex outputs by type before st_vary, and
the interpolated path converts back with f2fN after interpolation. The
flat path (load_input) only asserted that the load was 32-bit (compiled
out in a release build) and returned the 32-bit coefficient for a
16-bit load.

A half4 varying decorated Flat (a vertex colour, translated from Metal
[[flat]]) then compiled to a 32-bit value standing in for a 16-bit def,
and the backend aborted the whole process when it could not pack the
result ("Packing assertion failed ... unaligned reg"). Release Mesa
without 0001 aborts on the same pair with a different assertion
(value.size == AGX_SIZE_32). An abort in the driver's compiler takes
down the process that asked for the pipeline: QEMU and its guest.

Narrow the flat value by its type, f2fN for floats and u2uN
(truncation) for integers, matching how 0001 widened it.

diff --git a/src/asahi/compiler/agx_nir_lower_interpolation.c b/src/asahi/compiler/agx_nir_lower_interpolation.c
--- a/src/asahi/compiler/agx_nir_lower_interpolation.c
+++ b/src/asahi/compiler/agx_nir_lower_interpolation.c
@@ -129,12 +129,25 @@
       .io_semantics = nir_intrinsic_io_semantics(load));
 
    if (load->intrinsic == nir_intrinsic_load_input) {
-      assert(load->def.bit_size == 32);
-
       if (nir_intrinsic_io_semantics(load).location == VARYING_SLOT_LAYER)
-         return nir_load_layer_id(b);
+         return nir_u2uN(b, nir_load_layer_id(b), load->def.bit_size);
+
+      /* The coefficient registers hold 32-bit varyings: the vertex side
+       * widens 16-bit outputs by type before st_vary (agx_nir_lower_uvs).
+       * A 16-bit flat input (e.g. a SPIR-V Float16 varying decorated Flat)
+       * therefore reads a 32-bit value and must narrow it by its type, as
+       * the interpolated path below does with f2fN. Returning the 32-bit
+       * value for a 16-bit load left a mismatched def that the backend
+       * later failed to pack ("unaligned reg"), aborting the compile.
+       */
+      nir_def *flat = interpolate_flat(b, coefficients);
+      if (load->def.bit_size == 32)
+         return flat;
+      else if (nir_alu_type_get_base_type(nir_intrinsic_dest_type(load)) ==
+               nir_type_float)
+         return nir_f2fN(b, flat, load->def.bit_size);
       else
-         return interpolate_flat(b, coefficients);
+         return nir_u2uN(b, flat, load->def.bit_size);
    } else {
       nir_intrinsic_instr *bary = nir_src_as_intrinsic(load->src[0]);
 
